[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged **412 unique reports** (the export lists 427 rows because its
pages overlap; one id is one report). The merge was made on the subject line
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by cause, the reports hold
two different problems.

<Callout>
One fix will not close this ticket. Fixing the parser does not explain the 33 `hint` reports.
</Callout>

## What is in it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| # | Problem | Reports | Fix belongs to |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `parser` reads every date month first; day-first tenants get flipped dates | 379 | shared date parser: **fixed** (closed 05 Oct, "fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales") |
| 2 | `hint`: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people at day-first tenants (`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`) type month first | 33 | booking-v3 form hint: **won't fix**, the booking-v3 form is retired |

379 + 33 = 412. Five of the 379 describe a day off by one rather than a month flip (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620). The desk counts them under `parser`, so they are not a third problem.

## Why the first merge hid this

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant: where they
are and which booking form they run. Matching on subject cannot see either.

## Next

- Ticket 1 (379 reports) is closed as fixed. Ticket 2 (33 reports) is closed as won't fix.

